A||N||7||johnmac||Auto Transmission Cooler?||||1||
Z||000000||johnmac||07-20-2001||02:28 PM||||Has anyone installed an additional oil cooler for the auto transmission.<P>The side scoop on the driver side would provide a perfect cool air source. <P>Any comments?<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-20-2001||02:48 PM||||If you use the driver's scoop, you're going to be heating the intake air for the engine which will give you less power and increase the chance of detonation. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_24||07-20-2001||03:01 PM||||You should add scoops on both sides and add the cooler on the passenger side.  I am thinking of doing the same, but I heard they are only going to really do their job on a long trip or racing.  Maybe someone will have some actual written documentation in this forum, and if so I would be interested in seeing it.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||West Coast Fiero||07-20-2001||03:30 PM||||run a fairly large stacked-type cooler mounted on the front of the AC condenser in front of the car. Best effecientcy, also allows you to run the new lines in the original cooler line location||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnmac||07-20-2001||03:44 PM||||Has anyone done this installation?<P>I have big scoops on both sides on my GT. If the vented oil cooler is located directly in the air path, should be outside cool air.<P>There is a rubber recirc oil line on the Auto transmission a mere 12" away. Could I connect to this line?<P>Placing a Oil cooler ahead of the A/C condenser is ideal except for the long lines involved.<P>Any ideals?<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000005||isthiswhereiputausername?||07-20-2001||04:00 PM||||I'm running my tranny cooler up by my rad, Works great.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000006||johnmac||07-20-2001||04:38 PM||||Before the Radiator - Looks like this is the favoured location.<P>Any installation details?<P>Whose unit, hose sizing and etc.<P>What kind of thermal improvement do you see?<P>Thanks,<P>------------------<BR>John MacHaffie<BR>86GT "Yellowbird"<BR>12+ month project car<BR>johnmac@mpinet.net<BR>Winter Springs, Florida||||reg||1
Z||000007||grinthock||07-20-2001||04:58 PM||||I am running one, it made the tranny run smoother, and the engine ran a little cooler, it's a great cheap add-on RaceTech in Canada here did it for me the cooler was like $90....  Mounted with 2 straps up front, kinda like brackets....  ||||reg||1
